ountry></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIE, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI HEAVY INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERAICHI, TORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKORO, SEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIE KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERAICHI TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKORO SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIE, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERAICHI, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKORO, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A rotary drum type flying shear, wherein upper and lower rotary drums (13, 14) having shear blades (13a, 14a) are supported on a bearing frame (12) through eccentric sleeves (15, 16), respectively, so that only the upper rotary drum (13) can be rotated by a drive motor (17), the eccentric sleeves (15, 16) are rotated by a drive motor (25) so that the rotary drums (13, 14) can be moved toward and away from each other, interlocking gears (29, 30) are fixed to the shaft end parts of the rotary drums (13, 14), respectively, so that they can be interlocked with each other when the rotary drums are moved toward each other, and Oldham's couplings (41, 42) are installed between the interlocking gears (29, 30) and synchronizing gears (33, 34), respectively, so that the rotary drums (13, 14) can be rotated synchronously at all times.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une cisaille volante à tambour rotatif dans laquelle des tambours rotatifs supérieur et inférieur (13, 14) équipés de lames de cisaille (13a, 14a) sont disposés sur un corps de palier (12) à travers des manchons d'excentrique (15, 16) respectivement, de sorte que seul le tambour rotatif supérieur (13) puisse être actionné par le moteur d'entraînement (17). Les manchons d'excentrique (15, 16) sont mis en rotation par un moteur d'entraînement (25) de manière à rapprocher ou éloigner les tambours rotatifs (13, 14) l'un de l'autre. Des appareils d'enclenchement (29, 30) sont fixés aux parties d'extrémité de l'arbre des tambours rotatifs (13, 14) respectivement, de manière à s'enclencher solidairement lorsque les tambours rotatifs sont rapprochés l'un de l'autre. Des joints d'Oldham (41, 42) sont installés entre les appareils d'enclenchement (29, 30) et des appareils de synchronisation (33, 34) respectivement, ce qui permet de synchroniser en permanence la rotation des tambours (13, 14).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>